WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.560 --> 00:00:04.160
- A certified avalanche dog like Tali

00:00:04.160 --> 00:00:06.912
can do the work of about 30 rescuers

00:00:06.912 --> 00:00:08.309
in the same amount of time.

00:00:08.309 --> 00:00:11.883
Their sense of smell is
10 times greater than ours

00:00:11.883 --> 00:00:13.387
and if someone's buried in the snow,

00:00:13.387 --> 00:00:15.509
or not even buried but
just lost in the woods,

00:00:15.509 --> 00:00:17.557
the dog can smell their scent coming up

00:00:17.557 --> 00:00:19.851
through the snow pack and
tell me where to start

00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:22.550
digging to find that person.

00:00:22.550 --> 00:00:24.363
We are the first responders
and a lot of times

00:00:24.363 --> 00:00:27.429
if things go well into our training,

00:00:27.429 --> 00:00:29.050
we can facilitate that
rescue without putting

00:00:29.050 --> 00:00:31.802
anybody else in harm's
way, and be done quickly

00:00:31.802 --> 00:00:33.809
and efficiently and all go home safely.

00:00:33.809 --> 00:00:34.642
(barks)

00:00:34.642 --> 00:00:35.652
We gotta find somebody, I know.

00:00:35.652 --> 00:00:36.612
You want to find somebody?

00:00:36.612 --> 00:00:38.529
Okay Tali, let's go, search.

00:00:40.377 --> 00:00:41.444
My name's Hunter Mortenson.

00:00:41.444 --> 00:00:42.500
I'm an Avalanche Technician here

00:00:42.500 --> 00:00:44.814
at Breckenridge Ski
Resort with my ski patrol

00:00:44.814 --> 00:00:46.702
partner Tali, and we've been working here

00:00:46.702 --> 00:00:48.785
for eight years together.

00:00:49.870 --> 00:00:51.118
We're really fortunate
here at Breckenridge.

00:00:51.118 --> 00:00:53.582
We have six avalanche
rescue dogs on staff.

00:00:53.582 --> 00:00:55.910
Today Tali's here with her coworkers

00:00:55.910 --> 00:00:58.801
and friends is Boudreaux,
the Golden Retriever,

00:00:58.801 --> 00:01:01.958
and Ayup, another mountain purebred mutt.

00:01:01.958 --> 00:01:03.985
The years of the big Saint Bernard

00:01:03.985 --> 00:01:05.447
and Swiss mountain dog with the barrel

00:01:05.447 --> 00:01:07.623
under their neck, those dogs are built

00:01:07.623 --> 00:01:09.575
for the mountains, they're
sturdy, they're hardy,

00:01:09.575 --> 00:01:11.377
they can do it but what we're finding is

00:01:11.377 --> 00:01:12.743
they don't travel well in the snow

00:01:12.743 --> 00:01:15.697
and they're not as fast
moving across the snow.

00:01:15.697 --> 00:01:18.161
And avalanche rescue is all a matter of time

00:01:18.161 --> 00:01:20.071
and so we're looking these days for dogs

00:01:20.071 --> 00:01:21.820
that are a little bit on the smaller side,

00:01:21.820 --> 00:01:25.570
a little more nimble
and a little more quick.

00:01:27.463 --> 00:01:31.388
So the training, we start
them six to nine months old,

00:01:31.388 --> 00:01:33.639
and a lot of it is just basic obedience

00:01:33.639 --> 00:01:35.953
and then we start building
from the obedience

00:01:35.953 --> 00:01:38.727
into actual hide-and-go-seek type games.

00:01:38.727 --> 00:01:39.975
And then we build up from there

00:01:39.975 --> 00:01:41.991
into big snow caves where we'll bury

00:01:41.991 --> 00:01:45.596
a person almost six feet
deep if we have enough snow,

00:01:45.596 --> 00:01:47.303
and then the dog will start searching,

00:01:47.303 --> 00:01:49.159
having to find where
that scent's coming up

00:01:49.159 --> 00:01:50.129
to play the game.

00:01:50.129 --> 00:01:51.953
And all they're really
looking for is that person

00:01:51.953 --> 00:01:53.681
who they think has their toy.

00:01:53.681 --> 00:01:55.598
Ah, that's a good girl.

00:01:57.351 --> 00:01:59.847
It's about two full years of training

00:01:59.847 --> 00:02:02.172
to take your last certification test

00:02:02.172 --> 00:02:04.711
for an avalanche rescue dog and handler.

00:02:04.711 --> 00:02:07.324
So I'm certified to work with Tali.

00:02:07.324 --> 00:02:09.744
(barks)

00:02:09.744 --> 00:02:12.284
My whole last eight years of my career

00:02:12.284 --> 00:02:15.676
have been spent with
her every day all day.

00:02:15.676 --> 00:02:16.881
When we have to do our thing,

00:02:16.881 --> 00:02:19.036
we're really dependent on each other

00:02:19.036 --> 00:02:21.671
and I couldn't do what I do without her.

00:02:21.671 --> 00:02:23.463
And so it's an amazing partnership

00:02:23.463 --> 00:02:25.041
and I'm really honored and proud

00:02:25.041 --> 00:02:29.208
to be a part of this program
and work with a dog like her.

